# p_census_peak_s5_graphclear: diagnostic. p_census_peak_s5 with graph_clear_values_cpu added.
#
# (1)        inference hump (p_census_peak_s5, census at 97.9% of the peak):
#              188.7 MB  n=10   (768, 3072)          FFN weights
#              188.7 MB  n=40   (768, 768)           attention weights
#              178.2 MB  n=1    (22268928,)          the embedding, flat
#              169.9 MB  n=9    (3072, 768)          FFN weights
#               94.4 MB  n=5    (2359296,)
#               42.5 MB  n=9    (589824,)
#              --------
#              862.4 MB of WEIGHTS, against 317.7 MB of activations.
#            encrypt_spill_cpu reloads each share on Parameter.forward: the whole parameter set is back in
#            memory at the inference peak.
# (2)        graph_clear_values_cpu measures 0.02% twice (line operating point; allocator pinned).
# decides    weight rows shrink -> the lever reaches them (pages retained elsewhere); rows stand -> the
#            lever's _pending accounting misses parameter nodes (fixable).
# run        PEAK_TRIGGER_PCT=0 (as its pair).
# not a step probe_census_cpu records only.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu,graph_clear_values_cpu,probe_census_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
